    -> this red is a STALE PAGE, not the recipe: touching changes which
    pair is newest, so the landed band still quotes the previous newest
    pair and cannot print a recipe row for a pair it never saw. Honest
    reading: the board's completion test as literally written is not
    satisfiable by any writer, because the band is a snapshot.
  flip test after ONE re-render plus ONE injection (what the ring does
  inside a single pass):
    DELIVERABLE INDEX faces=9 fingerprint=1a26d80aece81b2f index=43230B
    VERDICT PASS 23/23 fingerprint=b906ec062cc8b071
    PASS AC-DIX21 mode=recipe rc=0/0 all-arms-green
    PASS AC-DIX23 mode=recipe all-arms-green
  note the size moved 43113B -> 43230B on that flip: the newest pair's
  NAME changed, which is content, not a number whose width wobbles. The
  numeric loop is gone; a flip still costs one re-render, which the ring
  already performs before its checks.

honest
  (a) this is a carrier invariant, not a product capability: no page a
      buyer can use appeared, and the shipped faces read the same content
      (the padded numbers render identically).
  (b) the fix removes the NUMERIC feedback edge only. Any window that
      changes index.html's size for a content reason still stales every
      face block that quotes it until backhop re-injects - that is the
      backhop step's job and it was already in the ring.
  (c) the criteria AC-BYI1..AC-BYI5 live in the pinned board row and are
      measured here; they are NOT yet registered as shipped suite arms
      (the suite count stays 23/23), so next window owes the registration
      if they are to be held by the battery.
  (d) ZERO payment capability, no network beyond loopback; the five
      physical pieces (merchant id, server, domain, filing+ICP,
      miniprogram appid+secret) are still missing - buyers still cannot
      pay.
